---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<DocsLayout locale="en" title="Five-minute quickstart" description="Create a least-privilege token, verify authentication, and ask your first grounded question." section="Getting started">
  <Fragment slot="toc"><a href="#token">Create a token</a><a href="#configure">Configure</a><a href="#verify">Verify</a><a href="#ask">Ask</a></Fragment>
  <h2 id="token">1. Create a token</h2><p>Sign in to E时代 RAG, open Personal Center → Agent API, and choose a name, scopes, and expiration. The full token is displayed once, so copy it immediately.</p>
  <h2 id="configure">2. Initialize configuration</h2><pre><code>emoera config init
emoera auth set-token</code></pre><p>The token prompt hides input and stores the credential in your OS keychain. For a self-hosted instance:</p><pre><code>emoera config set endpoint https://your-rag.example.com</code></pre>
  <h2 id="verify">3. Verify identity and capabilities</h2><pre><code>emoera auth status
emoera whoami
emoera capabilities</code></pre><p>A 401 means the token is invalid or expired. A 403 usually means the token is missing a required scope.</p>
  <h2 id="ask">4. Ask a question</h2><pre><code>emoera ask "Summarize our deployment policy"</code></pre><p>Interactive output shows the rewrite, retrieval, reranking, and generation stages. Use `--json` for machine consumption.</p>
  <div class="next-step"><div><b>Next</b><span>Understand scopes, keychains, and environment variables.</span></div><a href={`${base}/en/authentication`}>Authentication</a></div>
</DocsLayout>
